        "collapsible_tab_AN6y99": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "About Nationally Recognised Course",
            "icon": "star",
            "content": "<p>This is the highest qualification available in Australia and has been designed to give you all the skills and competency required to begin testing and tagging. This course has been completed by individuals, large corporations and hundreds of small and medium-sized businesses.</p><p>By completing the Nationally Recognised Course you will receive a statement of attainment for UEESS00174 - Electrical Safety Testing of Electrical Cord Connected Equipment and Cord Assemblies Skill Set.<br/><br/>This Skill Set contains the following Units of Competency which you will complete as part of this course:</p><p><strong>UEECD0007</strong> - Apply work health and safety regulations, codes and practices in the workplace</p><p><strong>UEERL0003</strong> - Conduct in-service safety testing of electrical cord-connected equipment and cord assemblies</p><ul><li><strong>Costs:</strong> $495 GST Exempt</li><li><strong>Duration</strong>: 1 day face-to-face (8-9 hours), plus online WHS component (3-4 hours)</li><li><strong>Locations: </strong>Brisbane, Gold Coast, Sunshine Coast</li><li><strong>Qualifications Received</strong>: Statements of Attainment & ID card with Certificate No.</li><li><strong>Qualification Level</strong>: Highest level (ASQA approved)</li><li><strong>Electrical knowledge: </strong>No previous electrical knowledge or background is required</li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_t9AL73": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "About Short Course (Non-Accredited)",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "content": "<p>The Short Course meets the minimum requirements set by AS/NZS 3760 and still allows you to freely test and tag as you wish. Although it also involves a face-to-face course over one day, it has some minor differences:</p><ul><li>No OHS component</li><li>Issued with Certificate of Attendance</li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_RUBEc8": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Course Detail",
            "icon": "clipboard",
            "content": "<p>Test & Tag Training is QLD's trusted provider of the highest level of fully accredited, nationally recognised training.</p><p>Courses held in Brisbane, Sunshine Coast and Gold Coast run from approx. 8:00am to 4:30pm.<br/><br/>On the day you'll be provided with everything you need, which includes a manual, pen, notepad and equipment to use (you can also bring your own portable appliance tester). <br/><br/>You will be shown how to use a PAT Tester in a small-sized class (strict maximum of 12 students) by an experienced test and tag industry specialist. This will ensure you have an interactive learning experience and given all the help you need. The course comprises of both theory and practical, but it does focus heavily on practical hands-on work to ensure you're completely ready to test and tag on your own. <br/><br/>Once you have completed the course, we place an emphasis on giving you free lifetime support. We'll be there to provide any technical help you might require across Queensland, whether it's by phone, email or by coming into our office.<br/></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_eYq8tp": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Locations",
            "icon": "map_pin",
            "content": "<h3>Brisbane:</h3><p>Construction Skills Training Centre,<br/>878 Beaudesert Rd Coopers Plains QLD 4108<br/></p><h3>Gold Coast:</h3><p>Housing Industry Association,<br/>Unit 4/2 John Duncan Court Varsity Lakes QLD 4227<br/></p><h3>Sunshine Coast:</h3><p>Dicky Beach Surf Club, <br/>1A Coochin St Dicky Beach QLD 4551</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_aUKp3U": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why Use Us",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "content": "<ul><li>We provide lifetime technical support after the course, available daily</li><li>We have conducted training for over 18 years in QLD with 2500+ reviews</li><li>Our Nationally Recognised Course is of the highest industry standard</li><li>We're a fully certified Registered Training Organisation</li><li>All of our instructors hold a min.  Cert IV in Training & Assessment</li><li>Course is delivered in an easy-to-understand and interactive manner</li><li>Anyone can do the course - you don't need to have any qualifications or electrical knowledge</li><li>Training focuses on practical, hands-on work</li><li>We teach the updated 2022 Standard AS/NZS 3760:2022</li><li>Special deals after the course if you would like to buy equipment</li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_PLAMRG": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Portable Appliance Testers (PAT's)",
            "icon": "lightning_bolt",
            "content": "<p>Test and Tag Training will teach you how to use the latest and most popular Portable Appliance Testers on the Australian market.<br/><br/>For students looking to buy a new PAT Tester, this will give you the opportunity to try a few different options and to choose the ideal one for your job. After the course we'll help you pick the best one based on your requirements.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
